  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Monolith vs Microservices: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Monolith vs Microservices: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Shapes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Monolith==: one deployable, one process, usually one database",
                "Modules call each other ==in-process==",
                "==Microservices==: small services, each owns one business function and its data",
                "They talk over the network: HTTP, gRPC, events"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Monolith",
                "Microservices"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Deploy",
                  "one unit",
                  "per service"
                ],
                [
                  "Calls",
                  "function call",
                  "network"
                ],
                [
                  "Data",
                  "one DB",
                  "DB per service"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Trade-offs",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Wins",
                "Fits / price"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Monolith",
                  "one deploy, local calls, ==ACID==, easy debugging",
                  "small teams, unclear domains"
                ],
                [
                  "Microservices",
                  "independent deploys, per-service scaling, team autonomy, fault isolation",
                  "{red:network failure}, {red:latency}, {red:distributed data consistency}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Modular Monolith",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One deployable with ==strict module boundaries==",
                "The usual best ==starting point==",
                "Cheapest path to splitting later"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Default",
              "text": "Start with a ==modular monolith==. Extract a service only when a clear pain appears."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why not microservices first?** Small team, unclear domain, wrong boundaries.",
                "**Price of microservices?** Network failure, latency, data consistency.",
                "**Modular monolith?** One deploy, strict module boundaries."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bounded Contexts and Business Capabilities",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Bounded Contexts and Business Capabilities",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bounded context",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Bounded context== (DDD): a boundary where a domain model and its terms have **one consistent meaning**",
                "Same word, different models: each context owns its own version"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Term",
                "Billing",
                "Shipping"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Customer`",
                  "payment method, invoices",
                  "address, delivery window"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Drawing the boundary",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Decompose by ==business capability==: Orders, Payments, Inventory, Shipping",
                "Capability = what the business **does**",
                "{red:Not} by technical layer: UI service, DB service",
                "Size rule: ==one team== owns it, changeable with **no coordinated release**"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Context map",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Relationship",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Customer/Supplier**",
                  "upstream supplies, downstream needs shape its API"
                ],
                [
                  "**Shared Kernel**",
                  "small model co-owned and changed together"
                ],
                [
                  "**Anti-Corruption Layer**",
                  "translates a legacy model so it does not leak in"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Legacy model",
                    "sub": "old terms",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ACL",
                    "sub": "translates",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New service",
                    "sub": "clean model",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Boundary test",
              "text": "One team, one capability, one bounded context."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Database per Service and Data Consistency",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Database per Service and Data Consistency",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Own Your Data",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Database per service==: only the owner touches its data",
                "Others use its **API** or **events**, never its tables"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Shared DB couples services by ==schema==",
                "One column change breaks several teams",
                "Blocks **independent deploys**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Queries Across Services",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use instead"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Cross-service join",
                  "**API composition**: query services, merge result"
                ],
                [
                  "Cross-service join, fast reads",
                  "**CQRS** read model built from events"
                ],
                [
                  "ACID across services",
                  "==Saga== (below)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Saga and Eventual Consistency",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Saga: local transactions, each with an undo",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Reserve stock",
                    "note": "undo: release",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Charge payment",
                    "note": "undo: refund",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ship order",
                    "note": "undo: cancel",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Choreography}: services react to each other's events",
                "{purple:Orchestration}: a coordinator commands each step",
                "==Outbox==: save DB change and event in one local transaction",
                "Consumers must be ==idempotent==: dedupe by event id"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Eventual consistency",
              "text": "Replicate data by **events**. If reservation fails after payment, the saga runs the ==compensating refund==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Strangler Fig Migration",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Strangler Fig Migration",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Pattern",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Strangler fig==: a **facade** (API gateway or reverse proxy) sits in front of the monolith",
                "Route traffic to new services ==one capability at a time==",
                "Old code shrinks until nothing is left to serve"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Facade",
                    "sub": "gateway / proxy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New service",
                    "sub": "migrated slice",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Monolith",
                    "sub": "everything else",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Loop",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Identify a seam",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Build new service",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Route a slice",
                    "note": "small % of traffic",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Verify",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Retire old code",
                    "note": "then repeat",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "First slice: ==low coupling==, **clear value** (notifications, search)",
                "Leave the ==tangled core== for last"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Data and Rollback",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Approach",
                "Verdict"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Dual writes",
                  "{red:Risky}: one write can fail, data drifts"
                ],
                [
                  "Change data capture",
                  "{green:Preferred}: stream DB changes to the new service"
                ],
                [
                  "Anti-corruption layer",
                  "{green:Preferred}: translates the legacy model"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Rollback and data",
              "items": [
                "Rollback = ==re-point the route==",
                "Main edge over a **big-bang rewrite**",
                "Migrate ==data ownership last=="
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Facade first, one slice at a time, verify before retiring, data ownership last."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes and Trade-offs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Mistakes and Trade-offs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Splitting Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Distributed monolith}: services must deploy together or share a DB",
                "Pays ==all the cost== of microservices, gets **none** of the benefit",
                "==Split too early==: guessed boundaries are costly to move",
                "Start with a **modular monolith**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Chatty Calls",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "one request",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Orders",
                    "sub": "sync hop",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pricing",
                    "sub": "sync hop",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Stock",
                    "sub": "sync hop",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Tax",
                    "sub": "sync hop",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each sync hop adds ==latency== and failure rate",
                "Five hops at 99.9% each give about 99.5% available",
                "Fix: **coarser services** or ==async events=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Ops and Team Fit",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Missing basic",
                "Why you need it"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Tracing",
                  "follow one request across services"
                ],
                [
                  "Centralised logs",
                  "one place to search"
                ],
                [
                  "CI/CD per service",
                  "independent deploys"
                ],
                [
                  "Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers",
                  "stop cascading failure"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Conway's Law==: architecture mirrors team structure",
                "Few engineers: a **monolith** is usually right"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Red flags",
              "text": "Lockstep deploys, a shared DB, or more services than engineers: you built a ==distributed monolith==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
